\b\i\fs36 Initiate Paths and Mysteries \par
\ul\i0\fs32\par

\pard\sl240\slmult1\fs28 Black Magic\par
\fs32\par
\ulnone\fs24 Warp Spell \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
School: Abjuration \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: A spell or mystery cast by someone else \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: Will negates; see text \par
Spell Resistance: No \par
You can cast this mystery as an immediate action to warp another caster\rquote s spell or mystery. In this case, warp spell must be used at the moment of the other casting. To be successful, you must beat the other caster on an opposed caster level check (1d20 + caster level). If you do not, you have failed to take control of his spell or mystery, and it manifests normally. If you succeed on the opposed check, the other caster\rquote s mystery or spell is countered, as if you had used the counter-spell action successfully, and you gain one additional use of an apprentice level mystery that you know. You can keep this additional use until a later turn (requiring a standard action to activate), but it must be used within 1 hour or it is lost. You can also combine the activation of the additional spell or mystery with the immediate action required for the warp spell mystery, allowing you to cast the apprentice level mystery out of turn.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Echo Spell \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
School: Universal \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Effect: Repeat a previously cast spell or mystery \par
Duration: See text \par
Saving Throw: See text \par
Spell Resistance: See text \par
You can echo a mystery or a spell cast by anyone other than yourself, causing it to remanifest under your control. Both the caster and the effect must have been within echo spell\rquote s range, and the entire casting must have occurred in the previous round. You can cast the mystery or the spell using your shadowcaster level level (use your Int modifier to determine the mystery or spell\rquote s DC, its duration, saves, and the like as normal for that mystery or spell). You cannot echo a mystery or spell of a higher level than the highest-level mystery you can cast, and you can never echo a mystery or a spell of higher than 4th level.\par
\fs24\par
\b Flood of Shadow \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
School: Abjuration \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Area: 20-ft.-radius spread \par
Duration: 10 minutes/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: None \par
Spell Resistance: See text \par
A flood of mystical shadow-power renders casting more difficult. To cast most spells while in, or cast spells into, an area affected by flood of shadow, the caster must succeed on a Spellcraft check (DC 15 + spell level), or the spell is lost with no effect. Mysteries or any spells of the shadow sub-school can be cast within or into the affected area without making the Spellcraft check. In addition, if a mystery or spell of the shadow sub-school originates in an area affected by flood of shadow, its variable numerical effect is increased by 50% (as if it was empowered), although its level does not increase.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Body and Soul\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Bolster \par
\b0 Level: 4th \par
\fs22 School: Transmutation \par
Range: Touch \par
Target: Creature touched \par
Duration: 10 minutes/level or until discharged (D) \par
Saving Throw: Will negates (harmless) \par
Spell Resistance: Yes (harmless) \par
You grant the subject 5 temporary hit points for each its Hit Dice (maximum 75 temporary hit points). For the duration of the effect, the subject\rquote s shadow grows larger than normal, and its movements are very slightly uncoordinated with those of the subject. An observer can notice this characteristic by making a DC 20 Spot check.\par
\fs24\par
\b Languor \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
Range: Close (25 feet + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Duration: 1 round/2 levels (D) \par
Languor functions like either the spell slow or the spell hold monster, except as noted above. You choose which version you want before the effect begins. If you choose hold monster, the mystery can affect only one subject.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Investiture \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
School: Transmutation \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: One creature \par
Duration: 1 round/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: Fortitude negates \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
You infuse the subject with the power contained in its own shadow. This grants the creature resistance to cold 15, the evasion ability, and darkvision 60 feet.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Dark Reflections\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Shadow Evocation \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
School: Illusion (Shadow) \par
This mystery functions like the spell shadow evocation, except as noted above. In addition, this mystery can mimic an evocation spell of 4th level or lower (rather than 5th level or lower).\par
\fs24\par
\b Feign Life \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
This mystery functions like the spell animate objects, but the items grow dark and warped, becoming more sharp edged and appearing slightly worn or decayed for the duration of the effect. The objects animated by this mystery also gain concealment.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Evocation, Greater \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
School: Illusion (Shadow) \par
This mystery functions like the spell greater shadow evocation, except as noted above. In addition, this mystery can mimic an evocation spell of 6th level or lower (rather than 7th level or lower).\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Ebon Roads\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Step into Shadow \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
This mystery functions like the spell dimension door.\par
\fs24\par
\b Pass into Shadow \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
This mystery functions like the spell plane shift, except that your destination or origination must be the Plane of Shadow.\par
\fs24\par
\b Voyage into Shadow \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
This mystery functions like the spell shadow walk, except as noted here. Your movement rate on the Plane of Shadow is double that described by the spell. Further, upon reaching your destination, you can attempt a DC 30 Knowledge (The Planes) check; success indicates that you appear exactly where you wish, rather than being shunted to a nearby space as per the spell. You need not leave the Plane of Shadow once you enter it, and this mystery can be used on the Plane of Shadow to travel rapidly.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Elemental Shadows\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Aura of Shade \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
School: Abjuration \par
Range: Touch \par
Target: Creature touched \par
Duration: 1 round/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: Will negates (harmless) \par
Spell Resistance: Yes (harmless) \par
You protect the subject from low temperatures and cold energy with a thin layer of that energy\rquote s shadowy reflection. This grants the subject immunity to normal extremes of temperatures and absorbs cold damage from attacks and effects. When an aura of shade absorbs a total of 12 points of cold damage per caster level (maximum 240), it expires. For as long as the aura is active, the subject\rquote s weapon or natural weapon melee attacks deal an extra 1d6 points of cold damage.\par
\fs24\par
\b Dark Air or Water \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
School: Transmutation \par
This mystery functions like the spell control water or control winds. You decide which version to use at the time of casting.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Storm \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
School: Evocation (Electricity, Cold) \par
Range: Medium (100 ft. + 10 ft./level) \par
Targets: One primary target, plus one secondary target/level (each of which must be within 30 ft. of the primary target) \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: Reflex half \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
This mystery creates a blast of electricity and cold energy, much like some of the fearsome weather found on the Plane of Shadow. The storm strikes one target initially, and then arcs to other targets. The storm deals 1d6 points of damage per caster level (maximum 20d6). Half of this damage is electricity damage, and the other half is cold damage. After it strikes, the storm arcs (like the spell chain lightning) to a number of secondary targets equal to your caster level (maximum twenty). The secondary arcs each strike one target and deal half as much damage as the primary one did (round down).\par
\par
\ul\b\fs28 Unbinding Shade\par
\ulnone\b0\fs22\par
\b\fs24 Shadows Fade \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
This mystery functions like the spell dispel magic, except as noted above.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Unravel Enchantments \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
This mystery functions like the spell break enchantment, except as noted here.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Shadows Fade, Greater \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
This mystery functions like the spell greater dispel magic, except as noted above.\par
\par
\ul\b\fs28 Veil of Shadows\par
\ulnone\b0\fs22\par
\b\fs24 Shadow Vision \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 4th \par
School: Transmutation \par
Range: Medium (100 ft. + 10 ft./level) \par
Target: One creature with an Intelligence of 3 or higher \par
Duration: 1 round/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: Will negates \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
You impede the subject\rquote s vision and its ability to determine what\rquote s happening around it. The subject takes a -4 penalty on attack rolls, ability checks, and skill checks. In addition, you have total concealment with respect to the subject (miss chance applies during each round of the duration).\par
\par
\b\fs24 Curtain of Shadows \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 5th \par
School: Transmutation \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Effect: Shadowy wall whose area is up to one 10-ft. square/level (S) \par
Duration: 1 minute/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: None \par
Spell Resistance: No \par
You create a wall of shadow that completely blocks line of sight. Any creature passing through the wall takes 1d6 points of cold damage per caster level (maximum 15d6).\par
\par
\b\fs24 Unveil \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 6th \par
School: Divination \par
Range: Touch \par
Target: Creature touched \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: Will negates (harmless) \par
Spell Resistance: Yes (harmless) \par
This mystery immediately ends any of the following adverse conditions: ability damage, blinded, confused, dazed, dazzled, deafened, diseased, exhausted, fatigued, immobilized, insanity, nauseated, sickened, stunned, and poisoned. In addition, it negates the effects of the mysteries mesmerizing shade, shadow hood, and shadow between, and cancels curses as the spell remove curse. \par
\par
\b\i\fs36 Master Paths and Mysteries \par
\fs32\par
\ul\i0\fs28 Breath of Twilight\par
\par
\ulnone\fs24 Life Fades, Greater \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 7th \par
School: Necromancy \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: One living creature/level in a 20-ft.-radius spread \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: Fortitude partial \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
You deal 1d6 points of damage per shadowcaster level and cause the subjects to become exhausted for 1 round per shadowcaster level (a Fortitude save reduces the damage by half and decreases the exhaustion to fatigue). This mystery does not stack with itself, so a creature fatigued by saving against one invocation does not become exhausted by saving against a second invocation.\par
\fs24\par
\b Flesh Fails, Greater \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 8th \par
School: Necromancy \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: One living creature/level in a 20-ft.-radius spread \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: None \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
This mystery functions like the mystery flesh fails, expect that you can affect multiple subjects, and you deal either 8 points of Strength damage, 8 points of Dexterity damage, or 4 points of Constitution damage. You must deal the same kind of ability damage to all subjects.\par
\fs24\par
\b Ephemeral Storm \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
School: Evocation \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: One living creature/2 levels, no two of which are more than 20 ft. apart \par
Duration: Instantaneous \par
Saving Throw: Fortitude partial \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
Targets of ephemeral storm must make a Fortitude save or die. Those who succeed take 5d6 points of damage.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Dark Metamorphosis\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Ephemeral Image \par
\b0 Level: 7th \par
\fs22 This mystery functions like the spell project image, expect as noted above. In addition, the image that you project has concealment unless it is in direct sunlight or within the area of a daylight spell or effect.\par
\fs24\par
\b Umbral Body \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 8th \par
School: Transmutation \par
Range: Personal \par
Target: You \par
Duration: 1 round/level (D) \par
You gain the incorporeal subtype and all advantages and traits associated with it.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Time \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
This mystery functions like the spell time stop.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Ebon Walls\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Prison of Night \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 7th \par
School: Conjuration (Creation) \par
Range: Close (25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels) \par
Target: One Huge or smaller creature \par
Duration: 1 round/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: Fortitude negates; see text \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
This mystery immobilizes the subject in a prison of shadow. This prison blocks both line of effect and line of sight to the creature inside it, and is impenetrable from the outside. The creature inside the prison takes 1d6 points of cold damage at the beginning of each round that it remains inside the prison. Once each round as a standard action, a creature caught in the prison can attempt a Fortitude saving throw against the spell\rquote s original DC to break out of the prison. Success means that the creature can move out of the prison, and it fade to nothingness. Failure means that the creature takes 1d4 points of Constitution damage and remains trapped.\par
\fs24\par
\b Tomb of Night \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 8th \par
This mystery functions like the mystery prison of night, except that instead of taking Constitution damage upon failing a Fortitude save to escape the prison, the creature gains one negative level. In addition, tomb of night deals 3d6 points of cold damage per round.\par
\fs24\par
\b Consume Essence \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
School: Necromancy (Death) \par
Range: Touch \par
Target: One living creature \par
Duration: Instantaneous, then 1 round/level (D); see text \par
Saving Throw: Will negates \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
The target of this horrid mystery must succeed on a Will saving throw or die. If the creature succumbs to the mystery and dies, it immediately returns to life at full hit points, but any spells it has already used remain expended. The creature is under your direct mental control. Each round you may issue instructions to the creature as a free action and it will carry out those instructions to the best of its ability. The creature remains in this state for 1 round per level, and then dies again.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Eyes of the Night Sky\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Truth Revealed \par
\b0 Level: 7th \par
\fs22 This mystery functions like the spell true seeing.\par
\fs24\par
\b Far Sight \par
\b0 Level: 8th \par
\fs22 This mystery functions like the spell greater scrying.\par
\fs24\par
\b Reflections of Things to Come \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
School: Divination \par
Range: Personal \par
Target: You \par
Duration: 10 minutes/level or until discharged \par
This mystery grants you knowledge of what will occur (or at least what is likely to occur), granting you several benefits. You gain the uncanny dodge ability, a +10 insight bonus on initiative checks (you always get to act in a surprise round), and a +4 insight bonus to Armor Class. In addition, you can discharge the energy of this mystery as an immediate action to cause an attack to miss you that would otherwise have been successful. You can declare that you are using this ability after the result of the attack roll is known, but you must do so before damage is determined. Using this ability discharges and ends the mystery. You can also discharge the energy of this mystery as an immediate action to immediately convert a failed saving throw into a successful one. Using this ability discharges and ends the mystery.\par
\fs24\par
\ul\b\fs28 Heart and Soul\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Dark Soul \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 7th \par
School: Enchantment (Compulsion; Mind-Affecting) \par
Range: Personal \par
Target: You \par
Duration: 1 round/level \par
Saving Throw: Will negates; see text \par
Spell Resistance: Yes; see text \par
You turn the dark energies from the Plane of Shadow upon another creature, compelling it to act in ways that it normally would not. While this effect is active, you can use a standard action to focus the shadow energies on one living creature within 30 feet that you select. The creature must succeed on a Will saving throw (DC 18 + your Int modifier) or immediately make a melee attack against one target chosen by you within its reach.\par
\fs24\par
\b Soul Puppet \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 8th \par
School: Enchantment (Compulsion, Mind-Affecting) \par
Range: Touch \par
Target: One living creature touched \par
Duration: 1 day/level (D) \par
Saving Throw: Will negates \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
The control granted by soul puppet follows the same mechanics as the spell dominate monster. Anyone observing the subject with the spell true seeing, the mystery truth revealed, or a similar ability sees tendrils of darkness extending a few feet from the subject before fading into nothingness. Similarly, anyone who observes you while directing the subject notices tendrils extending from your fingers, also fading into nothing.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Surge \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
Range: Close: 25 ft. + 5 ft./2 levels \par
Target: Up to one living creature/level, no two of which are more than 30 ft. apart \par
Duration: 1 round \par
Saving Throw: Will negates \par
Spell Resistance: Yes \par
This mystery functions like the spell dominate monster, except as noted above.\par
\par
\ul\b\fs28 Shadow Calling\par
\ulnone\b0\fs24\par
\b Summon Umbral Servant \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 7th \par
This mystery functions like the spell summon monster I, except as noted here. You can summon a greater shadow elemental or 1d3 huge shadow elementals. Shadow elementals use the statistics as fire elementals, but deal cold damage instead of fire damage.\par
\fs24\par
\b Shadow Plague \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 8th \par
School: Conjuration (Creation; Cold) \par
This mystery functions like the spell incendiary cloud, except that it deals cold damage rather than fire damage.\par
\fs24\par
\b Army of Shadow \par
\b0\fs22 Level: 9th \par
This mystery functions like the spell summon monster I, except as noted here. You can summon an elder shadow elemental or 1d3 greater shadow elementals. Shadow elementals use the statistics as fire elementals, but deal cold damage instead of fire damage. \b\i\fs28\par
\ul\i0\fs32\par
